{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Final disposition: `env_integration` (environment-induced) — CLOSING\n\n**Root cause:** ENOSPC / disk-pressure during the box-wide disk-fill incident tracked by P1 `5a05-0e52-33a0-48bf` (rebar-gerrit-data-disk-high). All 5 isolated single-hour `bridge_run_failures` (08-26 20:00; 08-27 15:00/19:00/22:00; 08-28 01:00 PDT) fall inside the `5a05` disk-pressure window (alarm open since 08-26 17:55 unrecovered; root-disk ~18 flaps, peak 98%, across 08-26..08-28). Under a full disk, either the reconcile child (a state write, or the store git commit of ticket events) or the delivery child (`rebar._store.push commit-and-push --strict`, `_bridge_runner.py:286`) hard-fails → OPERATIONAL_FAILURE → increments the metric; the next hour, with pressure momentarily eased, the pass succeeds — matching the scattered, self-clearing signature exactly.\n\n**No bridge/reconciler code defect.** Failing loud under ENOSPC is correct behavior: a pass cannot durably persist reconcile results or deliver ticket events to a full disk, and masking that as a reschedule would hide a real, data-affecting infra fault and blind `bridge_run_failures`. Will not recur once `5a05` disk pressure is remediated. Remediation is infra-lane (5a05), not reconciler code.\n\n**Confirmation basis:** on-box journald for the 5 timestamps was **unavailable** (the box ships no bridge logs to CloudWatch — only lmn-*/snap-* groups — and this session has no on-box access), so AC item 1 could not be executed directly. This close rests on the **accepted temporal correlation** to the `5a05` disk-fill window (all 5 failures inside it; ENOSPC mechanism; failing-loud-is-correct), which the orchestrator accepted in lieu of journald.\n\n**Linked:** `relates_to` `5a05` (a `caused_by` edge was refused because the incident ticket carries no referencing commit, and `--force` was not used). A separate follow-up ticket for the optional monitoring-contract enhancement (dampen nuisance alarm flaps from isolated transients) is filed and linked `discovered_from` this ticket — provenance only, left open for triage.\n\nClosing as `env_integration`, `caused_by` = the `5a05` disk-fill incident."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788065589643682731,"uuid":"b04d6718-b3c3-4ac9-8e99-6629c891cce9"}